 "description": "Heat fields: particles stamp brightness into a byte grid over the screen; every frame the grid is smoothed (4-neighbour average minus smooth_loss), optionally cleared cell by cell (a roll of 0..clear_range giving 0), and drawn as cell x cell Gouraud quads whose corner colours come from shade (colour word by brightness; missing entries are 0); runs where all four corners equal quiet_color are skipped; a draw-mode primitive (mode_*) closes the frame. emitter: burst (a disc thrown outwards, speed_scale * (speed_min + rand % speed_range), the third axis from fall_start by -gravity per frame down to fall_max), shell (a sphere at speed), cloud (a pool spawned on demand around a point, spread around it, throw = offset * spread_push + speed, lives life seconds, brightness_decay per second), fan (a screen-plane burst shown for lifetime seconds after it is armed), gather. follow_origin: the grid sits on the projected origin (else fixed on screen); stamp: added to a projected particle before the anchor is taken away; draw: the grid's top left corner relative to the anchor. Draw-order slot: (depth + depth_add) >> 1, + slot_add below slot_limit, else slot_far; each drawn row moves it by -row_slot_step. Times are Q12 seconds, speeds Q12. Each entry of \"fields\" is named; scripts and behaviours use the name. Every key is checked. A mod replaces the whole file with its own copy at the same path.",
